# Ignore everything in this directory, including public keys.
#
# This used to read `*` followed by `!*.pub`, on the reasoning that public halves
# are not secrets and are convenient to share. Both halves of that are true and
# it was still wrong, for a reason that has nothing to do with cryptography:
# provisioning INSTALLS whatever `.pub` files it finds here as authorized_keys.
#
# So a committed public key is not documentation — it is an access grant that
# ships with the repository. Three of them did, and two belonged to the same
# workstation. Anyone who cloned this repo and ran `docker compose up` got a
# container whose passwordless-sudo `admin` account, and whose default agent
# account, both trusted a key held by someone else entirely.
#
# Nothing in here is tracked now. Put your own keys here and they stay local,
# which is the behaviour the setup instructions always described.
*
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep
!README.md
